@startuml HermesCLI
title hermes-cli: high-level dependencies
top to bottom direction
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam nodesep 60
skinparam ranksep 65
hide empty members
class "main" as Main <<bootstrap>> {
  construct application objects and adapters
  inject selected implementations
  execute root command
}
package "Presentation" {
  class "internal/cli" as CLI {
    NewRootCommand
    auth / user / workspace / doc / inbox commands
  }
  class "internal/tui" as TUI {
    Model and screens
    polling lifecycle and terminal state
  }
}
class "internal/app" as App {
  Auth / Users / Workspaces / Documents / Inbox
  consumer-owned Remote and Store interfaces
  common operations for CLI and TUI
}
class "internal/editor" as Editor {
  Editor interface
  SystemEditor implementation
}
class "internal/model" as Models {
  User / Workspace / Document / Notification
  Session / Draft
  application errors
}
class "internal/client" as Clients {
  HTTPDocumentClient OR GRPCDocumentClient
  HTTPNotificationClient OR GRPCNotificationClient
  implement consumer-owned Remote contracts
}
class "Local adapters" as Local {
  FileConfigStore implements ConfigStore
  CredentialSessionStore implements SessionStore
  FileDraftStore implements DraftStore
}
class "External services" as Services {
  hermes-document-service
  hermes-notification-service
}
Main -down-> CLI : create and execute
CLI -right-> TUI : launch without arguments
CLI -down-> App : invoke
TUI -down-> App : invoke
CLI ..> Editor : foreground editor
TUI ..> Editor : suspend / resume terminal
App -down-> Clients : uses injected Remote contracts
App -down-> Local : uses injected Store contracts
App -left-> Models : shared types
Clients -down-> Services : selected network protocol
Clients -right-> Local : session lookup
note top of Main
  Creation happens here; runtime calls do not pass through main.
  All dependencies are explicit; no global mutable command tree.
end note
note bottom of App
  Auth uses AuthRemote and SessionStore.
  Users uses UsersRemote.
  Workspaces uses WorkspacesRemote and ConfigStore.
  Documents uses DocumentsRemote and DraftStore.
  Inbox uses InboxRemote.
end note
legend bottom
  Overview boxes group Go entities; they are not additional classes.
  App depends on interfaces, not on concrete adapter packages.
  Adapter implementation links: hermes-cli-clients.puml.
  Fake implementations are injected in application tests.
  One opaque session token; no refresh token.
  API transport and TUI library are not selected by this proposal.
endlegend
@enduml
